      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sales process was OK and they were fast in getting the bill for the deposit and the final payment out so they could be paid. The install date was postponed twice with very little notice provided. The second time it I was given less than 24 hours notice that it would be delayed again. The day before they had confirmed it would be fine.They ended up using a local electrical contractor to do the work and gave them the incorrect information. The guys who actually did the install have done a fine job but unfortunately they don't usually contract to the solar sales company.It would also be good if this company and others actually detailed the steps and processes that have to occur once the installation is completed. Don't think because the system is running your on solar. It may take up to 5 weeks to have the next two steps completed. These are done by the retailer and the energy provider and not the company you purchase the system from. But it would be good if they actually told you these additional steps as part of their sales process.No, I would not recommend Always Energy",
